meta {
  name: bKash Recurring RPP - Direct API (Sandbox)
}

vars:pre-request {
  bkashBaseUrl: https://gateway.sbrecurring.pay.bka.sh/gateway
  callbackUrl: https://<<<YOUR_DOMAIN>>>/api/v1/public/recurring-bkash/callback/SUB-REQ-TEST-001
}

script:pre-request {
  const apiKey = (bru.getEnvVar("bkashApiKey") || "").trim();

  if (!apiKey || apiKey === "PASTE_YOUR_API_KEY_HERE") {
    throw new Error("Set bkashApiKey in the active Bruno environment before sending requests.");
  }
  
  req.setHeaders({
    version: "v1.0",
    channelId: "Merchant WEB",
    timeStamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    "x-api-key": apiKey || "",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
  });
}

docs {
  # bKash Recurring RPP - Direct API (Sandbox)
  
  This Bruno collection mirrors the attached Postman collection and calls the bKash recurring API directly.
  
  ## Environment setup
  
  Use the included `Sandbox` environment and fill in only these credential values:
  
  - `bkashApiKey`
  - `bkashServiceId`
  - `bkashMerchantShortCode`
  
  Non-secret values such as the gateway base URL and callback URL are stored at the collection level. The request will fail immediately if `bkashApiKey` is missing from the active environment.
  
  ## Runtime variables
  
  These values are captured during a run and reused by later requests:
  
  - `subscriptionRequestId`
  - `bkashSubscriptionId`
  - `bkashPaymentId`
  
  If you run requests out of order, set the required runtime variable first or rerun the earlier request that populates it.
}